{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197654",
      "title": "Working with Route Parameters To Pass Data Between Screens",
      "lectureOrder": 98,
      "videoOrder": 94,
      "sourceHash": "24ba1e50cd2926cba349cb7918dabde35bb0da663b838cea2021812a271cbbfa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.043,
          "en": "So we got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.043,
          "end": 6.453,
          "en": "this basic forward-backward navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 10.5,
          "en": "One crucial thing is missing here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.5,
          "end": 12.7,
          "en": "at the moment we're not passing any data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.7,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "between these screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "and of course you don't always need to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "you often have navigation between screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 21.83,
          "en": "that don't need to pass any data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.83,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "But here we definitely wanna pass some information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "about the selected category to that Meals Overview Screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 32.87,
          "en": "Because for example, we maybe wanna show the category name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.87,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "in the header instead of this standard name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 38.68,
          "en": "but we'll talk about configuring headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.68,
          "end": 41.86,
          "en": "and so on later anyways, but most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.86,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "we wanna load the appropriate meals here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 46.373,
          "en": "on that Meals Overview Screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.53,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "Now, this is of course, a super common use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 52.39,
          "en": "and therefore passing data between screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.39,
          "end": 54.22,
          "en": "is extremely easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.22,
          "end": 57.74,
          "en": "You can do that with that navigate method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.74,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "that is exposed by the navigation prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.51,
          "en": "This navigate method takes the name of the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.51,
          "end": 66.03,
          "en": "to which you wanna navigate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.03,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "and this is required parameter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "But you also have an optional second parameter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 78.38,
          "en": "which you can pass in, which is actually an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "Now, this object which you pass as a second parameter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 85.66,
          "en": "allows you to define the params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.66,
          "end": 88.12,
          "en": "the parameters that should be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.12,
          "end": 90.31,
          "en": "to this to be loaded screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.31,
          "end": 92.963,
          "en": "so to the MealsOverviewScreen in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.95,
          "end": 97.233,
          "en": "And here you could pass a parameter called categoryId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.36,
          "end": 100.03,
          "en": "this name is up to you though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.03,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "this identifier is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "and then set the value for this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 109.67,
          "en": "In this case, I get my item data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.67,
          "end": 112.52000000000001,
          "en": "and we should keep in mind that item data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.52000000000001,
          "end": 115.64,
          "en": "is provided by a flat list in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.64,
          "end": 118.21000000000001,
          "en": "and therefore we have an item prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.21000000000001,
          "end": 120.52,
          "en": "And then on this item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.52,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "we have all the properties defined on a category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 126.76,
          "en": "So title, color, and ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.76,
          "end": 130.53,
          "en": "So therefore, we can get the idea of a category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.53,
          "end": 134.733,
          "en": "by using itemData.item.id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.7,
          "end": 139.14,
          "en": "And now we're passing the unique identifier of a category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 144.14,
          "en": "through that category param to the MealsOverviewScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.86,
          "end": 147.28,
          "en": "That of course brings up the next question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.28,
          "end": 151.78,
          "en": "how we can extract that value on that screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.78,
          "end": 152.993,
          "en": "that will be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "To extract parameters that are passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 160.61,
          "en": "with help of navigation, you go to the target screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.61,
          "end": 163.143,
          "en": "in this case, the mealsOverviewScreen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.99,
          "end": 167.38,
          "en": "And there we of course also get our navigation prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.38,
          "end": 170.69,
          "en": "so we can use object destructuring to pull that out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.69,
          "end": 173.25,
          "en": "off this prop object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.25,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "We get the navigation prop because this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 179.263,
          "en": "is registered as a screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.88,
          "end": 184.52,
          "en": "But we don't just get the navigation prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.52,
          "end": 189.35,
          "en": "You do get that if a component is registered as a screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.35,
          "end": 192.45,
          "en": "but you also always get a route prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.45,
          "end": 195.77,
          "en": "We didn't use that before, but now we will need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.77,
          "end": 198.82,
          "en": "So just like navigation, you get a route prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.82,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "in any component that is registered as a screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 204.62,
          "en": "with react navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.62,
          "end": 209.093,
          "en": "And this route prop here has a params property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.29,
          "end": 212.65,
          "en": "Now it also has a couple of other properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.65,
          "end": 215.99,
          "en": "and the best way to learn all about the available properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.99,
          "end": 220.31,
          "en": "is to go to the official docs, to the API Reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.31,
          "end": 222.84,
          "en": "And there you can learn and more about the navigation prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.84,
          "end": 225.5,
          "en": "which we used before, we'll take a look at some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.5,
          "end": 227.653,
          "en": "of its other methods later though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.55,
          "end": 230.74,
          "en": "And you'll also see the route prop there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.74,
          "end": 233.67000000000002,
          "en": "and there you see that on this route prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.67000000000002,
          "end": 236.46,
          "en": "you get params property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.46,
          "end": 240.67,
          "en": "which is actually an object containing the parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.67,
          "end": 243.67,
          "en": "that you might have passed to this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.67,
          "end": 245.38,
          "en": "You also get some other information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.38,
          "end": 247.27,
          "en": "like for example the name of the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.27,
          "end": 249.17,
          "en": "that was loaded if you need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.17,
          "end": 252.52,
          "en": "But in our case here, it's the params property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.52,
          "end": 253.833,
          "en": "which is very useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.28,
          "end": 257.62,
          "en": "So back here in MealsOverviewScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.62,
          "end": 261.595,
          "en": "we can use route params to get hold of the params object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.595,
          "end": 263.31,
          "en": "And the params object we get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.31,
          "end": 267.67,
          "en": "is param object we set up when navigating there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.67,
          "end": 272.39,
          "en": "So here we defined this params object when calling navigate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.39,
          "end": 275.5,
          "en": "In the MealsOverviewScreen, we now get this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.5,
          "end": 278.59000000000003,
          "en": "by accessing params on route therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.59000000000003,
          "end": 280.548,
          "en": "And hence, since I set categoryId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.548,
          "end": 283.64,
          "en": "as an identifier in this params object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.64,
          "end": 285.31,
          "en": "in the categories screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.31,
          "end": 289.38,
          "en": "we can use this same identifier here on this param object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.38,
          "end": 291.90999999999997,
          "en": "to extract that categoryId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.77,
          "end": 295.6,
          "en": "and I'll store it in a constant called catId here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 295.6,
          "end": 297.83,
          "en": "but of course, the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.83,
          "end": 300.6,
          "en": "So this is how we get the ID off the category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 304.453,
          "en": "that is passed through navigation to this new screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 305.44,
          "end": 307.52,
          "en": "And for the moment I just wanna output it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 307.52,
          "end": 309.68,
          "en": "so I'll just output it dynamically down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.68,
          "end": 311.44,
          "en": "in my text like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.44,
          "end": 314.883,
          "en": "so that we can see that we do get different values here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 315.98,
          "end": 317.58,
          "en": "With that if we go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 317.58,
          "end": 322.58,
          "en": "you see I got c1 here for Italian, for German it's c4,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 322.98,
          "end": 326.12,
          "en": "and for Asian it's c8.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.12,
          "end": 328.33,
          "en": "And these are the different IDs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 328.33,
          "end": 331.593,
          "en": "that are stored for the different categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.52,
          "end": 335.4,
          "en": "So that's how you can pass and extract parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "And this is a super common thing to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 341.14300000000003,
          "en": "and therefore it's of course important to notice pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.06,
          "end": 343.75,
          "en": "It's all the worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.75,
          "end": 347.04,
          "en": "that just as before with the navigation prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 347.04,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "you also have a hook which you can use use alternatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 352.34000000000003,
          "en": "to using the route prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 352.34000000000003,
          "end": 354.97,
          "en": "There's nothing wrong with using the route prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.97,
          "end": 356.68,
          "en": "but you can also import a hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.68,
          "end": 359.8,
          "en": "from @react-navigation/native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.8,
          "end": 362.773,
          "en": "and the hook which you wanna import is the useRoute hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 367.82,
          "en": "And just as before, this gives us a route object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.82,
          "end": 371.32,
          "en": "the same route object we get from props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 371.32,
          "end": 375.31,
          "en": "And then on this route object, we got our params and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 375.31,
          "end": 379.69,
          "en": "So you can use this hook as an alternative to this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.69,
          "end": 381.57,
          "en": "especially if you need access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 384.24,
          "en": "to the currently loaded route information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 384.24,
          "end": 386.4,
          "en": "in some nested component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 386.4,
          "end": 389.32,
          "en": "which is not registered as a screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.32,
          "end": 390.56,
          "en": "In screen components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.56,
          "end": 392.78,
          "en": "you can simply use the route prop instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 392.78,
          "end": 394.313,
          "en": "but you also don't have to.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
